# Heaven Furniture Mart - environment template
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Everything here is OPTIONAL: the page ships
# fully functional with no env at all.

# Meta (Facebook) Pixel id, digits only. Their marketing team runs FB/IG ads
# into this page; setting this wires the standard pixel (PageView) without a
# code change. Leave unset for zero third-party requests (the default).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are PUBLIC (inlined into the client bundle): never put a
# secret in one. A pixel id is public by design, so it is safe here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# The site's own origin, e.g. https://heavenfurnituremart.com - it signs every
# canonical, the sitemap and robots.txt. On Vercel this is unnecessary: the
# platform's own VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL is used. Set it when hosting
# anywhere else, or when a real domain replaces the vercel.app one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
